'' check.ti -- expression typing and operand legality.
''
'' The promotion rules here were MEASURED, not derived from the manual: every one of
'' the 3,920 (lhs, op, rhs) combinations in tests/types/expected/fbc-promotion.txt was
'' put to fbc as '#print typeof( a op b )', which fbc answers at compile time. That is
'' the frontend's own answer rather than something inferred from generated code.
''
'' What the table says, and none of it is what a C programmer would guess:
''
''   - Integers promote to INTEGER, which is POINTER-SIZED (64-bit here), not to the
''     32-bit LONG that C's integer promotions would give. 'ubyte + ubyte' is INTEGER.
''   - The result is UINTEGER only when an operand is itself 64-bit unsigned
''     (uinteger or ulongint). 'ulong + ulong' is INTEGER, because signed 64 holds
''     every unsigned 32 value.
''   - '/' is ALWAYS floating point -- 'long / long' is DOUBLE. Integer division is
''     the separate '\' operator.
''   - '^' is ALWAYS DOUBLE, even for 'single ^ single'.
''   - Comparisons yield INTEGER, not BOOLEAN. '=' and '<>' yield BOOLEAN only when
''     BOTH operands are already boolean.
''   - Arithmetic on BOOLEAN is rejected outright: 'boolean + boolean' is an error,
''     while 'boolean and long' is fine and yields INTEGER.

#ifndef __TKO_CHECK_BI__
#define __TKO_CHECK_BI__

#include once "tko.ti"
#include once "ast/nodes.ti"
#include once "symbols/symbol.ti"
#include once "symbols/resolve.ti"
#include once "symbols/redimrank.ti"
#include once "types/type.ti"
#include once "diag/engine.ti"
#include once "types/itable.ti"

namespace Tko.Check

    type Stats
        as int32 typed          '' expressions given a type
        as int32 untyped        '' reached, but no type could be determined
        as int32 badOperands    '' operand combinations fbc would reject
        as int32 callsResolved  '' calls bound to one overload
        as int32 callsAmbiguous '' calls with no single best candidate
        '' ONE UNTYPED ARGUMENT DECLINES THE WHOLE STATEMENT: the call is undecidable,
        '' so the callee never binds, so lowering has nothing to emit. Counting the
        '' argument's node KIND turns "some expression is missing" into a list of
        '' expression forms to implement, which is how PROCPTR was found.
        as containers.Array( of int32 ) argUntypedKind
        '' ... and the NAME at that leaf, when it has one. A kind says which shape is
        '' missing; the name says which one to write.
        as containers.Array( of uint32 ) argUntypedNames
    end type

    '' What one argument costs to pass to one parameter. Lower is better; CONV_NONE
    '' means the conversion does not exist and the candidate is not viable.
    ''
    '' The ordering was FITTED to tests/types/expected/fbc-overload.txt rather than
    '' derived: fbc's own ranking is not published, so the honest description is that
    '' this model reproduces every one of the 1,274 measured choices, not that it is
    '' the algorithm fbc runs.
    '' The tiers are separated by more than any within-tier distance can make up, so
    '' the ORDER is absolute: staying in the class beats changing it, widening beats
    '' narrowing, and only then does width distance decide. Each of those was forced
    '' by a measured row that a gentler separation got wrong.
    const CONV_EXACT    as int32 = 0
    const CONV_WIDEN    as int32 = 100      '' same class, no loss
    const CONV_NARROW   as int32 = 1000     '' same class, lossy -- always dearer than
                                           '' any widening, however far
    const CONV_CLASS    as int32 = 5000     '' integer <-> float
    const CONV_BOOL     as int32 = 20000    '' anything <-> boolean
    '' EVERY NUMERIC CONVERSION ALSO PAYS CONV_NUMERIC, and it matters only once there is
    '' more than one argument. fbc scores an argument FULL when it matches exactly and
    '' HALF less a closeness rank when it converts, and the gap between the two is wider
    '' than any two ranks can differ -- so a candidate matching one argument exactly beats
    '' one converting both, however cheaply. Without the tier the sum let two widenings
    '' (100 each) beat an exact match and a narrowing (1000): 'AddSaturating( long, -5L )'
    '' -- '-5L' is an INTEGER -- chose the LONGINT overload of fb/mathint.bi where fbc
    '' chose LONG. Added uniformly, it changes no single-argument order: every numeric
    '' conversion stays below CONV_BOOL, CONV_PTR_CLASS and CONV_USERDEF.
    const CONV_NUMERIC  as int32 = 10000
    '' A USER-DEFINED CONVERSION -- a conversion constructor on the destination, or an
    '' 'operator cast' on the source. Above every standard conversion and below
    '' CONV_NONE, and the standard conversion that follows it is ADDED rather than
    '' swallowed: measured, offered 'h( integer )' and 'h( double )' against a UDT that
    '' casts to integer, fbc picks the DOUBLE overload, so the second step still ranks.
    const CONV_USERDEF  as int32 = 200000
    const CONV_NONE     as int32 = 999999
    '' A TYPED VARIADIC'S EXPANSION, added once to a candidate that PACKS its arguments, so one
    '' that matches without packing always wins (docs/tiko-params/RFC-0001). Above CONV_NONE on
    '' purpose: it is added to a viable total, never compared with a single conversion.
    const CONV_EXPANDED as int32 = 5000000

    '' The POINTER tiers, measured in tests/types/expected/fbc-ptr.txt.
    ''
    '' An exact pointer type wins, 'any ptr' comes next, then a pointer whose POINTEE
    '' is the same width and class ('ulong ptr' for a LONG PTR argument, 'wstring ptr'
    '' for a SHORT PTR one), then everything else. That last tier is the one fbc warns
    '' about -- warning 3, 'Passing different pointer types' -- and warning 3 is also
    '' what makes a candidate unviable once the procedure is overloaded, which is the
    '' whole reason ConversionCost has to be told which question it is answering.
    '' DERIVED TO BASE, one tier per 'extends' link. Measured: an exact match wins, then
    '' the NEAREST base -- offered { object, T1, T2 } a T3 argument takes T2 -- and a
    '' base pointer BEATS 'any ptr', which is why this sits below CONV_PTR_ANY and the
    '' per-link step is small enough that 31 links still do.
    '' ADDING CONST IS ONE STEP, and only one. A 'byref x as const T' parameter takes a
    '' non-const T and must LOSE to an exact non-const overload when there is one:
    '' measured, offered { const T1, T1 } a non-const argument takes T1 and a CONST
    '' argument takes const T1, while offered only { const T1 } both take it.
    const CONV_CONST_ADD as int32 = 1
    const CONV_UDT_BASE  as int32 = 100
    const CONV_UDT_LINK  as int32 = 2
    '' ...BUT A UDT WHOSE CONST IS ADDED IS ONE TIER DOWN, as fbc scores any same-type
    '' match whose CONST differs: below EVERY derived-to-base conversion, whatever the
    '' depth (CONV_UDT_BASE + 30 links is 160), and above 'any ptr'. Measured: a T2
    '' offered { byref const T2, byref T1 } takes T1, a T3 offered { const T3, T1 } takes
    '' T1, and a 'T2 ptr' offered { const T2 ptr, T1 ptr } takes T1 ptr -- while offered
    '' { const T2 ptr, any ptr } it takes const T2 ptr. Adding const to a BASE is this
    '' tier plus one per link, so { const T2, const T1 } still takes const T2. For a
    '' non-UDT the step stays CONV_CONST_ADD: every numeric conversion is below fbc's
    '' demoted tier anyway, and a string has its own (CONV_STR_CONST_COPY).
    const CONV_UDT_CONST_ADD as int32 = 165
    const CONV_PTR_ANY   as int32 = 200
    const CONV_PTR_NEAR  as int32 = 250
    const CONV_PTR_OTHER as int32 = 400
    '' A TYPE, OR A POINTER TO ONE, TO AN INTERFACE IT IMPLEMENTS -- and an interface to one it
    '' inherits -- plus CONV_UDT_LINK per link (docs/tiko-interfaces §5.3, §17 Q8). Dearer
    '' than every derived-to-base pointer conversion, so 'f( byval p as Animal ptr )' beats
    '' 'f( byval a as IAnimal )' for a 'Dog ptr', as in VB: the class relationship is the
    '' more specific one.
    const CONV_IFACE     as int32 = 300

    '' A string converts to a pointer of its OWN string kind more cheaply than to
    '' 'string' itself, and to the other kind more dearly: a literal (which is
    '' ZSTRING * n) offered 'zstring ptr' and 'string' takes the pointer, while a
    '' STRING variable offered the same pair takes string.
    const CONV_STRPTR_SAME  as int32 = 50
    const CONV_STRPTR_OTHER as int32 = 150

    '' fbc's TIERS, for a var-len STRING argument, where they matter. From its tables
    '' (symb-proc.bas) and measured pair by pair: 'string' exact, then 'zstring' and
    '' 'zstring ptr' (the full tier, 100 and 150 here); then a SAME-type match whose
    '' CONST differs, either way round ('byref as const string' given a string, 'byval
    '' as string' given a const one), which fbc scores one tier down; then the half
    '' tier: 'ustring', 'wstring', 'wstring ptr' (CONV_STRPTR_OTHER + 10). So a string
    '' offered { byref const string, zstring ptr } takes zstring ptr, offered { byref
    '' const string, ustring } takes const string, and offered { ustring, zstring ptr }
    '' takes zstring ptr.
    const CONV_STR_CONST_COPY  as int32 = CONV_STRPTR_OTHER + 5
    const CONV_STR_TO_USTR     as int32 = CONV_STRPTR_OTHER + 6
    const CONV_STR_TO_WSTR     as int32 = CONV_STRPTR_OTHER + 7

    '' pointer <-> a pointer-sized integer. Dearer than the BOOLEAN tier because it
    '' loses to it: an INTEGER argument offered 'any ptr' and 'boolean' takes boolean,
    '' and a pointer argument offered 'any ptr' and 'integer' takes any ptr. Staying
    '' in the class wins on both sides.
    const CONV_PTR_CLASS as int32 = 50000

    '' 'overloaded' says whether more than one candidate is in play, because fbc asks
    '' two DIFFERENT questions and the answers differ. Called on its own, a procedure
    '' taking 'byte ptr' accepts a SHORT PTR argument with warning 3; add any second
    '' overload -- even a plainly unviable 'double' one -- and the same call is
    '' refused outright. Measured, not inferred: tests/types/expected/fbc-ptr.txt.
    '' The string element of a 'zstring * n' / 'wstring * n', or TYPE_NONE.
    declare function FixedStringElem _
        ( byval t as Tko.TypeId, byref types as Tko.TypeContext ) as Tko.TypeId

    '' A spelling the intrinsic table types -- see intrinsicname.tiko. Resolve, Check, the
    '' post-check argument sweeps and lowering all ask this one list.
    declare function IsTypedIntrinsicName( byref nm as string ) as boolean

    '' A NAME NOTHING DECLARED -- fbc's error 42. Run after Check, over the names Resolve
    '' could not bind; see undeclared.tiko. 'reserved' is '#pragma reserve''s list, whose
    '' names have an error of their own. 'isRtl' says whether an fb_ name is a runtime
    '' procedure -- the table is lowering's, a layer above, so the driver hands it in.
    type RtlNameFn as function( byref nm as string ) as boolean
    declare sub ReportUndeclared _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref names as Tko.Interner, _
          byref src as Tko.SourceManager, byref diags as Tko.DiagnosticEngine, _
          byref info as Tko.SemanticInfo, byref rst as Tko.Resolve.Stats, _
          byref reserved as containers.Array( of uint32 ), byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, _
          byval isRtl as RtlNameFn )

    '' The global 'operator ->' for a UDT and what it hands back. Both layers need
    '' them -- Check to TYPE 'p->v' and lowering to CALL the operator -- so they take
    '' the tables rather than a context.
    '' How good a numeric 'operator cast' is, for choosing among several. See the
    '' definition -- the ordering is measured and is not width.
    declare function NumericCastRank _
        ( byref types as Tko.TypeContext, byval t as Tko.TypeId ) as int32
    declare function ArrowOperatorFor _
        ( byref types as Tko.TypeContext, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, _
          byref names as Tko.Interner, byref ast as Tko.AstArena, _
          byref info as Tko.SemanticInfo, byval bt as Tko.TypeId ) as Tko.SymbolId
    declare function ArrowResultType _
        ( byref types as Tko.TypeContext, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, _
          byval op as Tko.SymbolId ) as Tko.TypeId
    declare function ConversionCost _
        ( byval from_ as Tko.TypeId, byval to_ as Tko.TypeId, _
          byref types as Tko.TypeContext, _
          byval overloaded as boolean = false ) as int32

    '' WHICH CONSTRUCTOR OR 'let' -- one resolver for Check and lowering (structpick.tiko).
    declare function StructorNamed _
        ( byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, byref names as Tko.Interner, _
          byval t as Tko.TypeId, byref which as string ) as Tko.SymbolId
    declare function StructorUserConvCost _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, _
          byref names as Tko.Interner, byref info as Tko.SemanticInfo, _
          byval at as Tko.TypeId, byval pt as Tko.TypeId ) as int32
    declare function StringSameWidth _
        ( byref types as Tko.TypeContext, byval a as Tko.TypeId, byval b as Tko.TypeId ) as boolean
    declare function CopyStructorOf _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, _
          byref names as Tko.Interner, byref info as Tko.SemanticInfo, byval t as Tko.TypeId, _
          byval defaulted as boolean ) as Tko.SymbolId
    declare function PtrCastScore( byref types as Tko.TypeContext, byval res as Tko.TypeId, byval dst as Tko.TypeId ) as int32
    declare function PtrCastBindsInSet( byref types as Tko.TypeContext, byval res as Tko.TypeId, byval dst as Tko.TypeId ) as boolean
    declare function NumCastParam( byref types as Tko.TypeContext, byval d as Tko.TypeId ) as boolean
    declare function NumCastBindsInSet( byref types as Tko.TypeContext, byval r as Tko.TypeId, byval d as Tko.TypeId ) as boolean
    declare function NumCastArgPick _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, _
          byref names as Tko.Interner, byval udt as Tko.TypeId, byval d as Tko.TypeId, _
          byref ties as int32 ) as Tko.SymbolId
    declare function PtrCastIsPick _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, _
          byref names as Tko.Interner, byval udt as Tko.TypeId, byval cast_ as Tko.SymbolId, _
          byval dst as Tko.TypeId ) as boolean
    declare function StructorCastCost _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, _
          byref names as Tko.Interner, byval at as Tko.TypeId, byval pt as Tko.TypeId ) as int32
    declare function UdtHasStrCast _
        ( byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, _
          byref names as Tko.Interner, byval udt as Tko.TypeId ) as boolean
    declare function CharRefCastPick _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, _
          byref names as Tko.Interner, byval udt as Tko.TypeId, byref charType as Tko.TypeId ) as Tko.SymbolId
    declare function PtrCastFit _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, _
          byref names as Tko.Interner, byval udt as Tko.TypeId, byval want as Tko.TypeId ) as int32
    declare function PtrCastPick _
        ( byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, byref names as Tko.Interner, _
          byval udt as Tko.TypeId, byval want as Tko.TypeId ) as Tko.SymbolId
    declare function NumericCastPick _
        ( byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, byref names as Tko.Interner, _
          byval udt as Tko.TypeId, byval want as Tko.TypeId ) as Tko.SymbolId
    declare function PickStructor _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, _
          byref names as Tko.Interner, byref info as Tko.SemanticInfo, _
          byval first_ as Tko.SymbolId, byref argT as containers.Array( of uint32 ), _
          byval tiesOut as int32 ptr = nullptr ) as Tko.SymbolId
    declare function LoneScalarStructor _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, _
          byref info as Tko.SemanticInfo, byval first_ as Tko.SymbolId, _
          byref argT as containers.Array( of uint32 ) ) as Tko.SymbolId

    '' WHICH 'operator cast' A STRING CONTEXT CALLS -- one rule, scored as fbc scores it
    '' (castpick.tiko). CR_*: what a cast yields; CT_*: the target a context asks with;
    '' CP_*: the outcome.
    const CR_NONE = 0, CR_STRING = 1, CR_USTRING = 2, CR_CHAR = 3, CR_CHARPTR = 4, CR_WCHAR = 5
    const CR_WCHARPTR = 6, CR_INT = 7, CR_FLOAT = 8, CR_OTHERPTR = 9
    const CT_STRING = 1, CT_USTRING = 2, CT_WSTRING = 3
    const CP_OK = 0, CP_NONE = 1, CP_AMBIGUOUS = 2, CP_NOCONV = 3
    declare function CastResultClass _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, _
          byval sym as Tko.SymbolId ) as int32
    declare function StrCastScore( byval target as int32, byval cls as int32 ) as int32
    declare function UdtStrCastFit _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, _
          byref names as Tko.Interner, byval udt as Tko.TypeId, byval target as int32 ) as int32
    declare function LitClassBuiltin( byref types as Tko.TypeContext, byval lc as int32 ) as Tko.TypeId   '' check.tiko, over lexer/littype.tiko
    declare function IntrStrOvlPick _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, _
          byref names as Tko.Interner, byval udt as Tko.TypeId, byval withUStr as boolean, _
          byref outcome as int32, byref outParam as int32 ) as Tko.SymbolId
    '' 'x casts to exactly that string type' (castpick.tiko).
    declare function UdtCastsToStr _
        ( byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, byref names as Tko.Interner, _
          byval t as Tko.TypeId, byval want as Tko.BuiltinType ) as boolean
    declare function StrCastPick _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, _
          byref names as Tko.Interner, byval udt as Tko.TypeId, byval target as int32, _
          byref outcome as int32, byref winCls as int32 ) as Tko.SymbolId

    '' Whether 'target = source' is allowed, and whether fbc warns about it.
    '' Assignment legality is a DIFFERENT question from binary promotion and does not
    '' follow from it: every numeric-to-numeric assignment is accepted, narrowing and
    '' all, without so much as a warning -- while 'long + string' and 'long = string'
    '' are both refused.
    enum AssignKind
        ASSIGN_OK = 0
        ASSIGN_WARN         '' allowed, but fbc warns -- pointer <-> pointer-sized int
        ASSIGN_REJECT
    end enum

    '' A folded constant. 'known' is false for anything this pass cannot evaluate --
    '' which is not an error, only an absence.
    type ConstVal
        as boolean  known
        as int64  value
        '' The WIDTH the value was folded at, 32 or 64. Not decoration: on win32
        '' 'integer' is four bytes, so '1 shl 31' is -2147483648 there and 2147483648
        '' here, and '&hFFFFFFFF' is -1 rather than 4294967295. Carried per sub-
        '' expression because a binary operator folds at the WIDER of its operands.
        as int32     bits
        '' UNSIGNED, from a 'u', 'ul' or 'ull' suffix and inherited by any operator
        '' with an unsigned operand. It changes COMPARISONS and nothing else: without
        '' it '&hFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFull > 0' folded as -1 > 0 and came out FALSE, which
        '' turned three passing '#assert' lines in the corpus into errors fbc does not
        '' have.
        as boolean  uns
    end type

    '' One folded value at a CONSTANT'S DECLARED width and signedness, read off its
    '' N_TYPEREF. A constant folds from its INITIALISER, and the initialiser knows
    '' nothing about the type it is being stored in: 'const v as ubyte = not u' is
    '' 255 to fbc and was -1 here. Pointers and proc types are returned unchanged.
    declare function ClampConstToTypeRef _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byval tref as Tko.NodeId, _
          byref v as ConstVal, byval intBits as int32 ) as ConstVal

    '' A float constant converted to an integer the way fbc folds it: half to EVEN.
    declare function RoundHalfEven( byval d as float64 ) as int64

    '' 'names' is OPTIONAL and enables one thing: folding an exact INTRINSIC over a
    '' constant ('abs( 42.3 )'), whose name has to be spelled to be recognised.
    declare function ConstFloatOf _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byval id as Tko.NodeId, byref outd as float64, _
          byval depth as int32 = 0, byval syms as Tko.SymbolTable ptr = nullptr, _
          byval scope_ as Tko.ScopeId = 0, byval names as Tko.Interner ptr = nullptr ) as boolean

    '' Fold an expression to an integer constant, matching fbc bit for bit. The
    '' source manager is needed for LEN and ASC, whose argument is a string literal
    '' recorded as a span rather than as text.
    '' 'intBits' is the width of INTEGER on the target -- 32 on win32, 64 elsewhere.
    '' It is the ONLY thing the evaluator needs from the target, and passing it keeps
    '' ConstOf independent of the symbol table, which is what matters: Resolve calls it
    '' before anything has been typed, for array bounds and 'zstring * N'.
    '' 'syms' and 'scope_' are OPTIONAL and enable one thing: folding a NAMED
    '' constant. Without them an identifier is simply not constant, which is the
    '' honest answer for a caller with no scope to look a name up in.
    '' 'types' and 'info' are for ONE question -- 'sizeof( T )' -- and both are optional
    '' for the same reason 'syms' is: a caller with no type context gets the honest answer
    '' for a caller with no type context, which is "not a constant".
    '' AN UNSUFFIXED DECIMAL LITERAL IS UINTEGER from 2^31 to 2^32 - 1 and from 2^63 up,
    '' INTEGER otherwise -- measured with fbc's '#print typeof': 2147483648, 3000000000 and
    '' 4294967295 are UINTEGER, 4294967296 is INTEGER, 9223372036854775808 is UINTEGER.
    '' A hex, octal or binary literal is not this rule's: '&hFFFFFFFF' is INTEGER.
    declare function DecimalLitUnsigned( byref lp as Tko.LiteralPayload ) as boolean
    declare function ConstOf _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byval id as Tko.NodeId, _
          byref src as Tko.SourceManager, byref names as Tko.Interner, _
          byval intBits as int32 = 64, byval syms as Tko.SymbolTable ptr = nullptr, _
          byval scope_ as Tko.ScopeId = 0, byval depth as int32 = 0, _
          byval types as Tko.TypeContext ptr = nullptr, _
          byval info as Tko.SemanticInfo ptr = nullptr ) as ConstVal

    declare function AssignableTo _
        ( byval src as Tko.TypeId, byval dst as Tko.TypeId, _
          byref types as Tko.TypeContext ) as AssignKind

    '' The type of 'lhs op rhs', or TYPE_NONE if the combination is not allowed.
    declare function BinaryResult _
        ( byval op as Tko.TokenKind, byval lhs as Tko.TypeId, byval rhs as Tko.TypeId, _
          byref types as Tko.TypeContext ) as Tko.TypeId

    declare function Run( byref u as Tko.FrontUnit, byref st as Stats ) as int32

    '' A LITERAL FORMAT STRING passed to std/strings' Format -- or any procedure taking a
    '' strings.FormatString and a typed variadic of strings.FormatArg -- checked against its
    '' arguments' kinds (formatcheck.tiko; docs/tiko-strings/RFC-0002-format.md section 7.1).
    declare sub CheckFormatStrings _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, byref types as Tko.TypeContext, _
          byref names as Tko.Interner, byref diags as Tko.DiagnosticEngine, _
          byref info as Tko.SemanticInfo, byref src as Tko.SourceManager )

    '' One line per PRINT argument: the source line, and the type computed for it.
    '' That shape exists so tools/gen/check-promo.sh can put tiko-lang's answer next to
    '' fbc's for the same 3,920 combinations.
    declare function Dump _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref src as Tko.SourceManager, _
          byref types as Tko.TypeContext, byref names as Tko.Interner, _
          byref info as Tko.SemanticInfo, byref st as Stats ) as string

    '' '--dump-decisions': one line per node with a recorded decision (SemanticInfo.decision)
    '' -- 'line:col KIND -> name@declline' -- the record lowering reads instead of choosing.
    declare function DumpDecisions _
        ( byref ast as Tko.AstArena, byref src as Tko.SourceManager, _
          byref names as Tko.Interner, byref syms as Tko.SymbolTable, _
          byref info as Tko.SemanticInfo ) as string

end namespace

#endif
